        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "58fe8ee9-2e8d-5490-8240-1ead2bf42127",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nathaniel Fillmore Jr., Millard Fillmore, Mary Abigail Fillmore, Zachary Taylor, Abigail Powers\n- Roles: American farmer, U.S. Representative, Vice President of the United States, President of the United States\n\nFacts:\n- Nathaniel Fillmore Jr. was born on April 19, 1771, and he was an American farmer.\n- Millard Fillmore was the son of Nathaniel Fillmore Jr. and later became the 13th President of the United States.\n- Millard Fillmore was a former U.S. Representative from New York before he was elected the nation's 12th Vice President in 1848.\n- Millard Fillmore became President of the United States after the death of Zachary Taylor.\n- Mary Abigail \"Abbie\" Powers Fillmore was born on March 27, 1832, in Buffalo, New York.\n- Mary Abigail Fillmore was the daughter of President Millard Fillmore and Abigail Powers.\n- Mary Abigail Fillmore died on July 26, 1854, in East Aurora, New York.\n- Nathaniel Fillmore Jr. died on March 28, 1863.",
